<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The cover image attached to every Play Games cloud commit (CLOUD-03, D-09): the app's own
  English-33 board art over its own violet field, composed here and rasterized at runtime by
  CoverImageSource.

  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS RATHER THAN RASTERIZING R.mipmap.ic_launcher — on API 26+ that id
  resolves to mipmap-anydpi-v26/ic_launcher.xml, an <adaptive-icon>, and AdaptiveIconDrawable
  .draw() applies its OWN mask. The cover would come out circle-cropped (or squircle-cropped,
  or teardrop-cropped) according to whatever the device's launcher last negotiated — a saves
  listing that looks different on two of the same player's phones for no reason they can see.
  This composite is deliberately UNMASKED and FULL-BLEED.

  It is also deliberately not a committed PNG. Both items below point at the existing vectors,
  so there is exactly ONE copy of the art in the tree and the cover cannot silently drift from
  the launcher icon. The mipmap-anydpi/ic_launcher.xml comment states the no-PNG rule for the
  whole repo; this file keeps it.

  The first item is the adaptive BACKGROUND vector and deliberately not its "..._legacy"
  sibling: that variant exists to give the API 24-25 square tile its own inset treatment, a
  launcher-tile concern with no meaning on a square cover.

  The foreground group is scaled 0.55 about centre for the adaptive safe zone, so the board
  occupies the middle ~55% here too. That is intentional: a cover cropped tight to the board
  would lose the violet field that makes the entry recognisable at listing size.
-->
<layer-list xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <item android:drawable="@drawable/ic_launcher_background" />
    <item android:drawable="@drawable/ic_launcher_foreground" />
</layer-list>
